@startuml arena
' SPEC: _spec/packages/starchess-arena/arena.puml
' HEADLESS SCRIPT ARENA — adjutant scripts play each other via the pure SCFEN engine; games recorded for replay.
' anchored to packages/starchess-arena/src/** and the core replay/economy files.
' covers: packages/starchess-arena/src/**
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/replay/**
' covers: packages/starchess-core/src/rules/economy.ts
' see also: _spec/apps/starchess/core/adjutant/cc-focus.puml (the ccIntel drop)
' see also: _spec/apps/starchess/core/adjutant/strategic/strategic-architecture.puml
!include ../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title StarChess · Script Arena — pure-engine match runner

package "packages/starchess-arena (pure, node/bun)" {
  component "runMatch\nbeginScTurn / endScTurn loop" as RUN <<app>>
  component "cli/main.ts\n--pairing --seeds --out" as CLI <<app>>
  package "players" {
    component "naive.ts\nadjutant() sync" as PW <<app>>
    component "strategic.ts\nstrategicAdjutant() + feed" as PS <<app>>
    component "core ai/strategic/tracking.ts\nseedKvsForOpening ·\nupdateKvsForSnap" as KVS <<engine>>
    component "core ai/strategic/tracking.ts\nseedCcIntelForOpening ·\nupdateCcIntelForSnap" as CCI <<engine>>
  }
  component "record.ts\nscfens + resolves" as REC <<app>>
  component "compare.ts\nsummarize → scoreboard" as CMP <<app>>
  component "feed/types.ts\nEngineFeed contract" as FEED <<host>>
  component "run/bank.ts\nmineral ledger" as BANK <<db>>
}

package "packages/starchess-core (pure SCFEN engine)" {
  component "beginScTurn · endScTurn\naddScAction · scOutcome" as CORE <<app>>
  component "adjutant / strategicAdjutant\ndeterministic scripts" as AI <<app>>
  component "rules/economy.ts\napplyStoredIncome · OPENING_STORED_MATERIAL" as ECO <<app>>
  component "replay/record.ts\nArenaGameRecord · historyFromRecord" as RCRD <<app>>
  component "replay/fen.ts\nSCFEN → classical-FEN projector" as RFT <<app>>
}

package "node service (Bun)" {
  component "StarChessFeed\n+ pool (implements EngineFeed)" as IMPL <<app>>
}

database "arena records\nin-memory capped (50)" as STORE <<db>>

RUN ARROW_MAIN CORE : beginScTurn → plan → endScTurn (per turn)
RUN ARROW_OPTIONAL BANK : seed · grantStoredIncome · debitSpend
BANK ARROW_MAIN ECO : applyStoredIncome
RUN ARROW_MAIN REC : { scfen, resolve } per settled ply
REC ARROW_MAIN RCRD : recordFromRun → shared schema
CLI ARROW_MAIN RUN : seeds · pairing · out dir
RUN ARROW_MAIN PS : plan(snap, {color, kvs})
RUN ARROW_MAIN PW : plan(snap, {color})
PS ARROW_OPTIONAL KVS : thread known-vs-seen
RUN ARROW_MAIN CCI : seed + update every settled ply
CCI -[#CB2000,dashed]-> PS : reaches SideContext,\n**never reaches adjCtx**
PS ARROW_OPTIONAL FEED : evaluate FEN projections
FEED ARROW_MAIN IMPL : getEvaluation (bounded movetime)
PS ARROW_OPTIONAL RFT : project classical FEN
AI ARROW_MAIN CORE : commit through addScAction only
REC ARROW_MAIN STORE : write record
RUN ARROW_OPTIONAL CMP : summarize(runs)

note bottom
  **Loop:** ""beginScTurn"" (sole turn-open owner; chip plies recorded with
  ""beginScTurn.next"") → per side ""script(snap)"" (fixed ""[w, b]"" order)
  → ""endScTurn({skipTurnStartChecks})"" → stored income → next turn.
  **Recording rule:** the settled ply is ""{ scfen: normalizeSnapGas(resolve.next),
  resolve }"" — never the pre-resolve snapshot — so ""resolves[i]"" produced
  ""scfens[i+1]"" exactly as the app replay expects.
  **Owned by the arena:** mineral bank ({w,b}) and per-side ""KnownVsSeen"".
  **Illegality is impossible by construction:** scripts commit via the core's
  ""addScAction"" gate; the engine only rescues candidate *scores*.
  **Termination:** ""maxTurns"" cap → draw by stall; both-null rejected;
  ""endScTurn"" throw → run marked aborted, never a crash.
  **Determinism:** ""engine:false"" + fixed ""mapSeed"" → equal scfens+resolves
  payloads (metadata excluded). The recorded resolves are authoritative for
  replay (replay never re-runs stockfish).
  **Gas refill:** no-chip turns advance to the gas-refilled turn-open snap
  (app parity: ""begun?.next ?? refillTurnGas(cur)"") so scripts plan with a
  real gas budget — the economy dials engage, not classical-only chess.
  `strategic.ts` is async and rescues candidate scores from an `EngineFeed`
  when a budget is attached; node ""StarChessFeed + pool + record store +
  routes"" live in _spec/apps/server/starchess-arena-feed.puml.
  **Web import:** file → localStorage + `?game=` + `?scfens=` validate before
  `historyFromRecord` → `ReviewDemoScreen` (_spec/apps/starchess/replay-import.puml).
  **Deploy horizon 5:** strategic economy projects bank 5 turns and scores
  `p+p+q` vs `n+b+r` at projected 11 to pick the Command Center drop.
end note

note as N_ROOKCAP
  **Why the engine may not boost every tank drop.** ""foldSuggestion"" folds a
  Stockfish ""cp"" into a candidate's deterministic score, capped at ±200 so one
  evaluation cannot outweigh the horizon bonuses the economy dials produce. A
  tank deploy gets a second, harder guard: when its landing file already holds
  a Marine, the engine suggestion is dropped entirely and the deterministic
  score stands.

  The reason is a known Stockfish bias — it over-values a rook on a file that
  classical chess would call open, and the SCFEN projection hides the StarChess
  reasons that file is worthless. The open-file test is a **coarse** placement
  scan, deliberately: it only has to de-prefer a blocked file, never to be
  exact, and a wrong answer costs a ranking nudge rather than a legal move.

  **A ""mateIn"" is absolute, a ""cp"" is advisory.** The perspective flips after
  our candidate, so a positive ""mateIn"" means the opponent mates us and earns
  ""-MATE_PENALTY"" outright. A ""timedOut"" suggestion is discarded — a partial
  evaluation never ranks anything.

  **Boosts are keyed by ""origIndex"", not by list position.** Candidates whose
  projection is ineligible are skipped, so the scored subset is sparser than the
  ranked list. Keying the boost map by the candidate's original index is what
  stops a skip from shifting a suggestion onto a neighbouring candidate, which
  would silently hand one move another move's engine score.
end note

note as N_OPEN
  <color:#CB2000>**OPEN — not fixed on this branch.**</color>

  **The strategic player discards the CC posterior.** ""runMatch.ts"" seeds
  ""ccIntel"" at line 123, refreshes it after every chip (142) and every settled
  ply (188), and hands ""ccIntel.perSide[color]"" to the player at line 168. But
  ""players/strategic.ts:85"" builds ""adjCtx"" as ""{ color, storedFor, kvs }"",
  so ""buildStrategicCtx"" falls back to ""emptyCCIntel(enemy)"" every turn.

  Consequence: the ""excluded"" set never accumulates, and a Hoverbike probe
  that proved a square empty is forgotten before the next ply. Arena results
  therefore measure a script whose CC search restarts each turn — which is
  **not** the script the strategic diagrams describe. Both paths are affected,
  plain and feed, because both use the same ""adjCtx"". Detail in
  ""_spec/apps/starchess/core/adjutant/cc-focus.puml"".
end note

PS .. N_ROOKCAP
PS .. N_OPEN
@enduml